  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0150 database is a comprehensive system for managing a community-driven platform, where users can create and share stories, engage in discussions through comments, and participate in moderation activities. At the heart of the system are the users, who are identified by a unique ID, username, email, and password, and can be administrators or banned from the platform. Each user can create stories, which are associated with a title, description, URL, and a score that reflects their popularity. Stories can be moderated, hidden, or saved by users, and their moderation status is tracked through the moderation logs. Users can also vote on stories and comments, which are linked to the respective stories and users. Comments are associated with a story and a user, and can be created, updated, and deleted. The platform also features a tagging system, where users can assign tags to stories, and a messaging system, where users can send and receive messages. Additionally, the system tracks invitations sent to users, and stores internal metadata and schema migration history.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\nThe project involves the development of a technology-focused community platform for link aggregation and discussion, similar to Hacker News. The platform, named Lobsters, is designed to cater primarily to enthusiasts and professionals in technology, programming, and computer science. It operates with an invite-only model to ensure high-quality content and discourse.\n\n 2) Objectives\n- To provide a platform for sharing and discussing links related to technology, programming, and computer science.\n- To maintain a high standard of content quality through an invite-only membership system.\n- To enhance community transparency with a public moderation log.\n- To facilitate community replication by operating as open-source software.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Community Members: Users who submit links and participate in discussions.\n- Moderators: Users responsible for content moderation and maintaining community standards.\n- Administrators: Users with elevated privileges to manage platform operations.\n- Visitors: Non-members who can view content but not participate.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- User Registration and Management: Support for invite-based user registration and profile management.\n- Content Submission: Users can submit links to articles, research papers, and blog posts.\n- Discussion Threads: Users can engage in threaded discussions related to submitted content.\n- Voting System: Users can vote on stories and comments to influence content visibility.\n- Tagging System: Stories can be tagged for improved categorization and searchability.\n- Story Moderation: Tools for moderators to manage content quality, including moderation logs.\n- Messaging System: Direct messaging capabilities for communication between members.\n- Story and Comment Management: Functions for saving, hiding, and moderating stories and comments.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Scalability: The platform should efficiently support growth in user base and content volume.\n- Security: Implementation of robust security measures, including encrypted passwords and data protection.\n- Performance: Ensuring low latency for user interactions, even with increased load.\n- Transparency: Access to public moderation logs to uphold community standards.\n- Usability: Intuitive user interface and navigation to promote ease of use.\n- Open-Source Accessibility: Available for other communities to replicate and adapt.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0150.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0150\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `is_admin` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `is_banned` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stories` (\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`story_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stories_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comments` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `votes` (\n  `vote_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `vote_type` enum('up','down') NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`vote_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`comment_id`) REFERENCES `comments` (`comment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tags` (\n  `tag_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`tag_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `story_tags` (\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `tag_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`story_id`, `tag_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `story_tags_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `story_tags_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`tag_id`) REFERENCES `tags` (`tag_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `messages` (\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `sender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receiver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `sent_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `messages_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `messages_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`receiver_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `invitations` (\n  `invitation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `sender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receiver_email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `sent_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`invitation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invitations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `moderation_logs` (\n  `log_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `moderator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `action` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `timestamp` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`log_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `moderation_logs_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `moderation_logs_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`moderator_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `schema_migrations` (\n  `version` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`version`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
